<h2>What you see</h2>

<p>Each view is a slice through a room with an outside wall and a window. You change a few inputs and watch how the picture shifts in the model.</p>

<ul>
    <li><strong>Air in the room.</strong> A radiator below the window. Colors show which air is cooler or warmer than the average room air, markers show how the air moves. You choose the window, the wall, the radiator setting and the outside temperature.</li>
    <li><strong>Cool walls and mould.</strong> The temperature of the inner wall surface and a risk estimate in three levels, with a range. You enter the outdoor temperature, the room temperature, the humidity in the room and a wall template. In development.</li>
</ul>

<h2>What it is, and what it is not</h2>

<p>The app calculates wall temperatures as steady-state heat conduction with common boundary conditions, based on common design values, not checked against standard texts. The air movement is a simplified two-dimensional picture and qualitative only. Every view carries a badge that says which simplifications apply. The details are on the <a href="/method/">method</a> page, short answers under <a href="/faq/">questions and answers</a>.</p>

<p class="notice">If you can see mould: consult a qualified building surveyor.</p>

